"""Mutation check: each deliberate bug, planted in a copy of a project, must make the
project's tests fail. A bug that the tests let through shows a missing test.

    python mutation/mutate.py mutation/.work [PART_OF_A_NAME] [lighthouse-memory|backend]

WORK_DIR is made and removed for every bug. PART_OF_A_NAME runs only the bugs whose name
holds it. The tests run against the FalkorDB of `docker compose up -d`, each on a graph of
its own; no bug may name a graph that holds real data.

Each bug is (name, file, text, replacement): the text must be in the file exactly once. The
tests most likely to catch a bug in a file run first, and the whole suite only if they
pass. It takes about an hour for all of them.
"""

